WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Build with Accessibility: opening the signed Android 1.0.0 release.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:22.000
The full disclosure explains screen content, screenshots, local storage, and auditing. Continue is disabled until consent.

3
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Choose Not now. The auditor opens with screen access disabled.

4
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Open Accessibility settings returns to the disclosure. Consent is still unchecked.

5
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Agree to screen access, then open Android Accessibility settings and select Build with Accessibility.

6
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Android asks for confirmation before enabling the accessibility service.

7
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Choose the optional floating capture control, then open a synthetic test screen and trigger a capture.

8
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:21.000
The service captures screen evidence and runs accessibility checks locally.

9
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:29.000
The predicted reading order is approximate. Actual TalkBack testing remains necessary.

10
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Review captured conditions and findings with confidence, severity, and fix guidance.

11
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:44.000
Finding details identify the affected control in the captured screen.

12
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Use the manual checklist for tests that automation cannot complete.

13
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Saved sessions keep audit captures and results together.

14
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.200
Keyboard focus is visibly outlined. Audits stay on the device until the user exports them.
